form4.spinedit9.hint="A ghost that comes back is invulnerable for this time."
form4.spinedit8.hint="Flame length of the bomb a ghost throws."
form4.spinedit7.hint="Hit points of all players that are not in the handicap table."
form4.spinedit6.hint="After a hit that is not lethal the player is invulnerable for this time, so the same flame does not hit twice."
form4.spinedit5.hint="Longest invulnerable time. The time is random between min. and max."
form4.spinedit4.hint="Shortest invulnerable time. The time is random between min. and max."
form4.spinedit36.hint="How long a bomb has to stay in the beam without a break until it is ignited. 0 = at once."
form4.spinedit35.hint="How long an opponent has to stay in the beam without a break until being hit."
form4.spinedit34.hint="How far the beam reaches. It stops at bricks, solid blocks and bombs."
form4.spinedit33.hint="How long a player can fire with one item. Only used up while firing, more items add fuel."
form4.spinedit32.hint="Share of the items below the bricks that become a flamethrower at the start of a round."
form4.spinedit31.hint="How long it takes until the screens are normal again."
form4.spinedit30.hint="How long the screens stay white."
form4.spinedit3.hint="Share of the disease items that make the player invulnerable instead of sick."
form4.spinedit29.hint="How white the screens get: 100 = nothing can be seen any more."
form4.spinedit28.hint="Share of the items below the bricks that become a white bomb at the start of a round."
form4.spinedit27.hint="How long it takes until the screen is normal again."
form4.spinedit26.hint="How long the screen stays white."
form4.spinedit25.hint="How white the screen gets: 100 = nothing can be seen any more."
form4.spinedit24.hint="Share of the disease items that turn the screen white. Rolled after the positive effects."
form4.spinedit23.hint="After a punch the same player cannot punch again for this time, so nobody can be stunned all the time."
form4.spinedit22.hint="Longest stun time. The stun time is random between min. and max."
form4.spinedit21.hint="Shortest stun time. The stun time is random between min. and max."
form4.spinedit20.hint="Seconds after the start of a round until the borders open, so nobody flees from the start corner at once. 0 = from the start."
form4.spinedit2.hint="Longest stun time. The stun time is random between min. and max."
form4.spinedit19.hint="Seconds after the start of a round until the teleporters appear and work, 0 = from the start."
form4.spinedit18.hint="How see-through the player is drawn: 0 = normal, 100 = invisible."
form4.spinedit17.hint="Longest time. The time is random between min. and max."
form4.spinedit16.hint="Shortest time. The time is random between min. and max."
form4.spinedit15.hint="Share of the disease items that let the player walk through bricks. Rolled after the positive disease."
form4.spinedit14.hint="All players are invulnerable for this time at round start."
form4.spinedit13.hint="Round time in seconds, hurry starts at 80 s remaining. 0 = time from the game settings."
form4.spinedit12.hint="Ghosts are visible for 3 ticks and invisible for 1 tick, this is the length of a tick. 0 = no flicker."
form4.spinedit11.hint="A ghost that hits no opponent within this time vanishes, 0 = unlimited."
form4.spinedit10.hint="How often a player can become a ghost per round, 0 = unlimited."
form4.spinedit1.hint="Shortest stun time. The stun time is random between min. and max."
form4.label9.caption="Invulnerable after a hit (ms)"
form4.label8.caption="Players survive several hits, set per player name. During hurry every hit is lethal."
form4.label7.caption="Max. invulnerable time (ms)"
form4.label63.caption="Time to ignite (ms)"
